course: dictionary
lesson: 15903
title: Unmask
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unmask is a verb. The word starts with un-, which often means taking something off, and mask is a covering for the face. So to unmask someone is to take off their mask so you can see who they really are.
explain: Unmask also has a second meaning. «The reporter unmasked the company's lies, and everyone learned the truth.» Lies and truth are the clues here. To unmask a person or a plan is to show the truth about them, especially when they are pretending to be something they are not.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. «The children pulled off the monster's mask and unmasked the caretaker» means the first meaning, a real face under a mask. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «show the truth» fits, you have found the second meaning.
fact: Unmask means to take off a mask, so you can see the face underneath.
fact: Unmask also means to show the truth about someone who is cheating, spying or doing wrong.
fact: The verb changes its ending: «unmasks» (now), «unmasked» (before), «unmasking» (happening).
fact: «Unmasked» is often used in stories and cartoons when the villain is revealed at the end.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The children pulled off the monster's mask and unmasked the caretaker.» What does unmasked mean here? | Hid his face behind a new mask | *Took off the mask to show his face | Ran away from the monster | Painted his face green
exercise: «The reporter unmasked the company's lies, and everyone learned the truth.» What does unmasked show? | *The truth about the lies | A cheap bag of sweets | A new mask for a party | The company's new office
exercise: Find and copy the word that means to show the truth about someone who has been pretending. «The detective unmasked the spy who had been pretending to be a friend.» | detective | pretending | *unmasked | friend
test: «Scooby-Doo always unmasks the villain at the end.» What does unmasks mean? | Makes a new costume for the villain | *Shows who the villain really is | Sings a happy song | Runs away from the villain
test: «The fake doctor was unmasked when the nurse noticed his papers were false.» Why was the fake doctor unmasked? | Because he was asked to sing | Because he took off his white coat for a rest | Because he won a prize at school | *Because the truth about him came out
exam: «Ella said the plan was a trick, and her teacher unmasked it in front of the whole class.» What does unmasked mean in this sentence? | Hidden under a new plan | Made the plan bigger | *Showed the truth about the plan, so everyone knew it was a trick | Forgot the plan
